# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THIS REPO — everything below is specific to the pi workspace
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── PER-HOST STATE: written independently on the laptop and on the VPS ─
# Nothing here is synced. Every pattern below is a file or folder that one
# host rewrites on its own — pi settings stores, trust decisions, bot tokens,
# caches, dashboards, ledgers, verdicts. Tracking any of it makes the next
# push/pull collide, so the rule is: if the runtime writes it, it lives here.
# Inventory, evidence and the conflict table:
#   agent/docs/runbooks/host-parity-laptop-vps.md
# Add a new path here the first time it shows up as a per-host change.
#
# pi's own per-host files (the agent home)
agent/auth.json
agent/telegram.json
agent/model-rates.json
agent/models-store.json
agent/default-model.json
agent/trust.json
agent/front-and-center.md
agent/git/
#
# trust decisions, at any depth (every sibling home writes its own)
**/trust.json
#
# sibling agent settings — each home has its own model/theme/extension choices
agent-web-master/web-master/settings.json
agent-web-master/web-master/default-*.json
agent-tasks-agent/tasks-agent/settings.json
agent-gog-workspace-agents/sm-google-workspace/sm-google-workspace/settings.json
agent-image-describer/image-describer/settings.json
agent-template-new-agent/template-new-agent/settings.json
#
# Telegram bot config + bridge runtime state, at any depth
**/telegram.json
**/tmp/pi-telegram/
#
# session, log and live state
**/sessions/
**/logs/
agent/tmp/
agent/pi-web-access/
agent/state/prompt-capture/
agent/observability/
#
# control-plane store (which mode/phrase is on differs per host)
# The *.sample.json copies are the tracked schema. Seed or reset a machine with:
#   cd ~/.pi && cp config.sample.json config.json \
#     && cp input-phrase-config.sample.json input-phrase-config.json \
#     && cp prompt-build-config.sample.json prompt-build-config.json
# Anchored to the repo root: nested config.json files stay tracked.
/config.json
/input-phrase-config.json
/prompt-build-config.json
#
# cron store and run history
cron/jobs.json
cron/runs/
#
# dashboards (pid files are per host and rewritten on every start)
.dashboard-logs/
#
# decision-node runtime (verdicts, sweep logs, message text kept 14 days)
decision-nodes/**/verdicts.jsonl
decision-nodes/**/logs/
decision-nodes/**/__pycache__/
decision-nodes/review.jsonl
# reminder store — per host, so a reminder made on one host stays there
decision-nodes/reminder/reminders.jsonl
#
# model catalog cache, at any depth (agent dirs, sub-agents)
models-store.json
#
# last archive-to-target run (one move, machine-local)
apps-scripts/archive-to-target-full-tree/archive-to-target-full-tree/archive-to-target-full-tree.last.json

# ── Sibling agent homes ───────────────────────────────────────────
# These rules used to live in five separate .gitignore files (one per agent home).
# Consolidated here so a single list governs the repo; the vendored projects under
# apps-scripts/ keep their own, because that layout is not ours.
**/default-model.json
**/front-and-center.md
agent-image-describer/**/model-rates.json
agent-tasks-agent/**/model-rates.json
agent-template-new-agent/**/model-rates.json
agent-web-master/**/model-rates.json
agent-web-master/**/tool-rates.json
# image-describer drops screenshots and dashboard builds next to its source
agent-image-describer/images/
agent-image-describer/**/dashboard/dist/
agent-image-describer/**/docs/archive/images/
agent-image-describer/**/.cursor/
agent-image-describer/**/.cursorignore
# web-master keeps a scratch npm dir
agent-web-master/web-master/npm/*

# ── Lockfiles that DO travel (they define the install on both hosts) ──
# Overrides the blanket `package-lock.json` rule above so the two locks that
# pin the agent install are versioned. Everything else stays ignored.
!agent/package-lock.json
!agent/npm/package-lock.json
# The tree itself is still per-host:
agent/npm/node_modules/

# ── This repo's local artifacts, scratch dirs and nested repos ─────
agent/bin/
sessions-summarizer/summarizer-state.json
sessions-summaries/
sessions-summaries/**
sessions-memory/
sessions-slim/
postgres-migration/**
web-search-cache/
z.old/
# agent-lan-agent is a standalone git repo (own history, own .gitignore).
# Tracked here only until 2026-11-03; the nested repo would otherwise be
# picked up as an untracked directory by every status call.
agent-lan-agent/
# explore-discover-pi is a separate checkout, not part of this repo
explore-discover-pi/
# removed agents kept for reference (004-style copies)
keep-agent-copy/**
agent#copy/

# ── Skills ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# skill-creator, video-finder, yt-download, pi-prompt-dump and
# agent-replica-adapt are git submodules (see .gitmodules); agent-creator and
# svg-photo-convert are plain directories tracked by this repo.
# Initialise a clone with: git submodule update --init --recursive
